{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a stitch task (#5295) from the cobbler-scaffold code generation pipeline. The task is to implement srd028-uniq requirements R4.1 through R4.4 (Exit codes and SIGPIPE) in cmd/uniq/main.go and add corresponding differential test cases to cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go. The specific requirements are:\n   - R4.1: Must exit 0 when all inputs are processed successfully\n   - R4.2: Must exit 1 when any input file cannot be opened, printing error to stderr\n   - R4.3: Must exit 1 when a write error occurs on stdout\n   - R4.4: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n   \n   Design decisions specify: extend existing implementation (don't rewrite), use differential testing with guniq reference binary via pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests, skip tests if guniq not found. No git commands allowed (orchestrator-managed).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests comparing Go binary against GNU guniq\n   - SIGPIPE handling via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Exit code conventions (0 for success, 1 for errors)\n   - Buffered I/O with bufio.Writer for stdout\n   - Custom argument parsing (no cobra - hand-rolled flag parser)\n   - The uniq utility operates on adjacent duplicate lines only (does not sort)\n   - NormalizeFunc pattern for normalizing error message differences between Go and GNU implementations\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd028-uniq.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for requirements R4.1-R4.4\n     - R4.1: Exit 0 on success\n     - R4.2: Exit 1 on file open error, print to stderr\n     - R4.3: Exit 1 on stdout write error\n     - R4.4: SIGPIPE handling via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n     - Non-goals: no --group flag, no sorting\n\n   - **cmd/uniq/main.go** (294 lines, existing implementation)\n     - Already has SIGPIPE handler at line 30: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n     - Already exits 0 on success via `run()` returning 0 (line 248) and `os.Exit(exitCode)` (line 41)\n     - Already exits 1 on file open error via `openInput()` error handling (lines 146-150)\n     - Already exits 1 on write errors: `emitRun` returns error → `deduplicate` returns 1 (lines 233-234), `w.Flush()` error returns 1 (lines 245-247), and main's `w.Flush()` error causes `os.Exit(1)` (lines 38-40)\n     - Key functions: `main()`, `parseArgs()`, `parseFlags()`, `run()`, `openInput()`, `openOutput()`, `comparisonKey()`, `deduplicate()`, `emitRun()`, `runCopies()`\n     - Options struct: `count, repeated, allRepeated, unique, ignoreCase, skipFields, skipChars, checkChars`\n\n   - **cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go** (499 lines, existing tests)\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"guniq\")` with skip pattern\n     - Has normalizers: `normalizeBinaryName`, `normalizeErrCase`, `normalizeOpenPrefix`, `normalizeTryHelp`\n     - Already has tests for R4.1: `r4_1_exit_0_success`, `r4_1_exit_0_file`\n     - Already has tests for R4.2: `r4_2_nonexistent_file`, `r4_2_extra_operand`, `r4_2_invalid_option`\n     - Missing explicit tests for R4.3 (write error on stdout) and R4.4 (SIGPIPE)\n     - Helper function: `writeFile(t, dir, name, content)`\n     - Test fixture files created: abc.txt, dups.txt, allsame.txt, nodups.txt, single.txt, empty.txt, trailing.txt\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Analysis of existing code reveals R4.1-R4.4 are largely already implemented in main.go:\n     - R4.1 (exit 0): Implemented via `deduplicate()` returning 0 and `os.Exit(exitCode)`\n     - R4.2 (exit 1 on file error): Implemented via `openInput()` error path\n     - R4.3 (exit 1 on write error): Implemented via error returns in `emitRun()`, `deduplicate()`, and main's `w.Flush()`\n     - R4.4 (SIGPIPE): Implemented via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` call at start of main\n   - The main remaining work is adding test cases. R4.3 and R4.4 are difficult to test via differential testing since they involve I/O error conditions and signal handling. Some tests already exist for R4.1 and R4.2.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extensive stitch task prompt with full project context, SRDs, architecture, constitutions, coding standards, constraints, and task description for implementing srd028-uniq R4.1-R4.4\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Determine if any code changes are needed in cmd/uniq/main.go for R4.1-R4.4 (analysis suggests the code already implements these requirements)\n   - Add differential test cases to cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go covering R4.1-R4.4 (especially R4.3 write errors and R4.4 SIGPIPE)\n   - Run `go build -o bin/uniq ./cmd/uniq/` to verify compilation (AC3)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/uniq/ -count=1` to verify tests pass (AC4)\n   - Verify existing R1.x-R3.x functionality is not broken (AC5)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three required files (SRD, main.go, uniq_test.go) and was about to begin implementation. The analysis shows:\n   - main.go likely needs minimal or no changes since R4.1-R4.4 are already implemented\n   - uniq_test.go needs additional test cases for R4.3 and R4.4 (possibly additional R4.1/R4.2 edge cases)\n   - The task acceptance criteria require: all four R4.x requirements implemented (AC1), differential tests added (AC2), successful build (AC3), passing tests (AC4), no regression (AC5)\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write modifications to cmd/uniq/main.go (if any needed) and add test cases to cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go for R4.1-R4.4. The existing code already implements the core R4 requirements, so the main work is adding test cases. For R4.3 (write error) and R4.4 (SIGPIPE), I would need to consider what differential test cases are feasible — SIGPIPE can potentially be tested by piping to a process that exits early (e.g., `head -1`), while R4.3 write errors are harder to trigger via differential tests. After writing code, run `go build -o bin/uniq ./cmd/uniq/` and `go test ./cmd/uniq/ -count=1` to verify.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5295/3cde0789-9cb3-4853-b792-04f28cc93281.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3cde0789-9cb3-4853-b792-04f28cc93281","uuid":"480182ad-cec5-4c11-a9b4-3b7771cee796","timestamp":"2026-05-19T21:34:28.863Z","isSynthetic":true}
